-- title:
--   The cost recurrence (round six, `cH_rec`)
-- statement:
--   **The cost recurrence.** For `e ≥ m`, `c(e) = (e mod m) + K₀ + (1/W) Σ_w c(w ⌊e/m⌋)`, the sum
--   over all children (`C.widths`).
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.R6BitCost`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem IntMul.Kappa.R6.Bit.cH_rec (C : QHNet R W T m) (hruns : C.RunsOK) {e : ℕ} (he : m ≤ e) :
--       cH C e = ((e % m : ℕ) : ℝ) + K0 C + (C.widths.map fun w => cH C (w * (e / m))).sum / W
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** Round six, bit side: cost of `progH` and the generalized Prop. 11
--
--   `costH C e V`: the structural cost of `progH C q e …` on an array of volume `V`, following the
--   program: `e < m`: `e` digit-swap passes; `e = m f + r`: `r` digit-swap passes, the row split and
--   merge (`2V`), `T` zero temporaries (`T V / W`), each gate one pass per touched wire (`V / W`),
--   each edge `4m` shift passes (`V / W` each) plus its run children, each a recursive call of width
--   `r' f` on a stream of volume `V / W`.
--
--   * `costH_lin`: `costH e V = V · costH e 1`.
--   * `cH_rec`: `c(e) = (e mod m) + K₀ + (1/W) Σ_{children} c(w ⌊e/m⌋)` (`c = costH · 1`).
--   * `costH_bound`: with `histMoment C.hist m τ < W`, `costH e V ≤ K V e^τ` for all `e` (via the
--     monotone majorant of `c` and `R6.MomentRec.moment_recurrence_bound`).
--   * `prop11H`: denotation and cost together.
--
